Keeps a key from replacing the prototype of the object that `transformKeys` and
`deepTransformKeys` build: assigning a `__proto__` key, which a transform can return and data
parsed with `JSON.parse` can have, replaces the prototype of the result instead of creating a
property. Both now define such a key as an own property, after converting the key like a property
access does, so a key that only converts to `__proto__`, like `["__proto__"]`, is caught too.
`replaceKeys` and our `transformKeysDeep` are affected, while the case conversions can't return
`__proto__`. The latest release (2.3.1) still has this bug.

